00:27:38.000 --> 00:28:03.000
So this is a really interesting question. It's also a challenge you wanted to answer scientifically. If we really wanted to find the answer, we would somehow randomly assign people to not answer study questions for a period of time and follow them and also look at people who are answering them. So I can't give a really rigorous scientific answer. All I can give you are the anecdotal evidence that we have from participants. So we asked them what their experience was like participating.
这是一个非常有趣的问题。这也是一个你想从科学角度回答的挑战。如果我们真的想找到答案，我们会以某种方式随机分配一些人，让他们在一段时间内不回答研究问题，并跟踪他们，同时观察那些正在回答问题的人。所以我无法给出一个非常严谨的科学答案。我能给你的只是我们从参与者那里得到的轶事证据。所以我们询问了他们参与研究的体验是怎样的。

47
00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:47.000
And most of them talked about it as a very positive experience. They talked about being able to kind of check in with themselves, thinking about where they were spending their time, how they were doing. I think, again, from many of these participants born in the early 19th century, this was an opportunity to talk about experiences that they were really socialized not to talk about. And in fact, they told us that they shared experiences with us that they never talked about with other people. So we think this sort of regular check-in might have some benefits for anyone, not just people in a study. And part of what we do in the good life is share some exercises and assessments like the assessments in the study that anyone can use to check
他们中的大多数人谈到这是一种非常积极的体验。他们谈到能够审视自己，思考他们把时间花在了哪里，他们过得怎么样。我认为，对于许多出生在19世纪初的参与者来说，这是一个谈论他们实际上被社会化教育而不敢谈论的经历的机会。事实上，他们告诉我们，他们与我们分享了从未与其他人谈论过的经历。所以我们认为这种定期的自我审视可能对任何人都有好处，不仅仅是研究中的人。我们在《美好生活》中所做的一部分工作就是分享一些练习和评估，就像研究中的那些评估一样，任何人都可以用来进行自我审视，

48
00:28:47.000 --> 00:29:17.000
in, particularly around their social functioning. So in the book, we highlight this idea about social fitness being really important. And like physical fitness, we need to exercise those muscles. So we provide some exercises that people can do to check in once a year or more regularly if they feel like they can use that support. But this connection people had to the study, It was quite extraordinary, and you see it partly from their sense that it helped them. We also have, we have, you know, file drawers full of information about the participants,
特别是在他们的社会功能方面。所以在书中，我们强调了社会适应能力非常重要的观点。就像身体健康一样，我们需要锻炼这些肌肉。因此，我们提供了一些练习，人们可以每年进行一次自我审视，如果他们觉得需要这种支持，可以更频繁地进行。但是人们与这项研究的联系是非常非凡的，你可以从他们认为这对自己有帮助的感觉中部分地看到这一点。我们还有，你知道，装满参与者信息的档案柜，

