all the questionnaires they were filled out. But we also have letters from the participants and letters from their families. And people were quite devoted to the study. It became an important part of their life. Some of these men and their families decided to donate their bodies and their brains to the study, which is an ultimate, you know, kind of example of sacrifice for others. And importantly, in addition to that incredible compliance for the first generation, when we went to the children of the original participants, almost two-thirds of them said, yes, I'd love to participate in that study that my parents have been participating. I've always been curious what kinds of questions you all ask.
所有他们填写的问卷。但我们也有来自参与者及其家人的信件。人们对这项研究非常投入。它成为了他们生活中重要的一部分。其中一些男性及其家人决定将他们的身体和大脑捐献给这项研究，这是一种为他人牺牲的终极例子。重要的是，除了第一代人令人难以置信的配合之外，当我们联系原始参与者的子女时，近三分之二的人说，是的，我很乐意参加我父母一直参与的那项研究。我一直很好奇你们问的是什么样的问题。

50
00:29:53.000 --> 00:30:20.000
So, yes, I'm happy to participate. So when you talk to the children, they were then accepted into the study in the same way that the original participants were? So it wasn't they were just reflecting upon their fathers, but they became subjects as well. Exactly. Exactly. So both of those things were important. We did ask them about their memories of growing up and these families that we follow very closely because that allows us to look at the difference between our retrospection and our eyewitness reports.
所以，是的，我很乐意参加。那么当你和这些子女交谈时，他们是以和原始参与者同样的方式被纳入研究的吗？所以他们不仅仅是在回顾他们的父亲，他们也成为了研究对象？完全正确。完全正确。所以这两件事都很重要。我们确实询问了他们关于成长过程中的记忆，以及我们密切跟踪的这些家庭，因为这使我们能够观察我们的回顾与目击者报告之间的差异。

